Apple's new iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max largely build on last year's models with a series of targeted upgrades rather than a major redesign. The most notable changes dial in better performance, camera capabilities, battery life, and wired charging speeds.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/What-Upgrading-to-iPhone-18-Pro-From-iPhone-17-Pro-Gets-You-Feature-2-1.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1064589" /><br/>
Several key specifications remain unchanged from the iPhone 17 Pro models. The iPhone 18 Pro and Pro Max retain the same 6.3-inch and 6.9-inch display sizes, 3,000-nit peak outdoor brightness, and 48-megapixel Ultra Wide and Telephoto cameras with 4x Telephoto and 8x optical-quality zoom.<br/>
<br/>
MagSafe and Qi2 charging also remain capped at 25W, while the overall industrial design – minus the Dynamic Island – is largely unchanged. The Main camera, however, receives substantial upgrades, including the new variable-aperture system. Here's what you can expect if you're planning to upgrade from an iPhone 17 Pro or Pro Max.<br/>
<ul><br/>
  <li>A20 Pro chip replaces the A19 Pro, with up to 20% faster CPU and 40% faster GPU performance.</li><br/>
  <li>7-core GPU that's up from the 6-core GPU in the A19 Pro.</li><br/>
  <li>Twice the AI processing performance, with a new Dual 16-core Neural Engine.</li><br/>
  <li>Redesigned vapor chamber with three times the surface area, enabling up to 40% better sustained performance.</li><br/>
  <li>Smaller Dynamic Island that can display up to three Live Activities at once.</li><br/>
  <li>Variable-aperture 48MP Main camera with ƒ/1.48, ƒ/1.8, ƒ/2.8, and ƒ/4 settings, replacing the fixed ƒ/1.78 aperture on the iPhone 17 Pro models.</li><br/>
  <li>Around 50% better low-light performance from the Main camera.</li><br/>
  <li>New manual camera controls for aperture, shutter speed, white balance, and histogram.</li><br/>
  <li>New Apple Reference Image feature for creating authenticated, unalterable reference photos.</li><br/>
  <li>Photographic Styles 3, with new texture and grain controls.</li><br/>
  <li>Cinematic effects that can now be applied after capture to video shot at up to 60 fps.</li><br/>
  <li>Cinematic mode at up to 4K Dolby Vision at 60 fps, up from 30 fps on the previous models.</li><br/>
  <li>Time-lapse recording upgraded to 4K Dolby Vision.</li><br/>
  <li>Improved Audio Mix with higher-quality voice processing and music isolation.</li><br/>
  <li>New smart focus tracking for photos and video.</li><br/>
  <li>Improved low-light video recording at 1080p.</li><br/>
  <li>Up to 36 hours of video playback on iPhone 18 Pro, up from 33 hours on the 17 Pro.</li><br/>
  <li>Up to 45 hours of video playback on iPhone 18 Pro Max, up from 39 hours on the 17 Pro Max.</li><br/>
  <li>Faster wired charging: Apple says 50% in around 15 minutes, down from around 20 minutes.</li><br/>
  <li>2TB storage option on the 6.3-inch iPhone 18 Pro, up from a 1TB maximum.</li><br/>
  <li>New Black, Silver, Glacier, and Burgundy finishes, replacing Silver, Cosmic Orange, and Deep Blue.</li><br/>
  <li>Heavier design: The iPhone 18 Pro is 5g heavier than its predecessor, while the iPhone 18 Pro Max is 16g heavier.</li><br/>
  <li>&#36;100 higher starting price: &#36;1,199 for iPhone 18 Pro and &#36;1,299 for iPhone 18 Pro Max.</li><br/>
